integ5 0081 = patches/exl3r/0067-exl3-decode-4-bit-grouped-experts-read-every-trellis-word-once.patch (overnight 2026-10-31), renumbered for the integrated stack on 3f94715d.

exl3 decode: 4-bit grouped experts read every trellis word once, and decode with fewer instructions (exl3r, 2026-10-31)

The grouped decode kernel's lanes each loaded the two 32-bit words their 16-bit windows span, so every trellis word was
fetched twice (prof5's NCU: 69-71 MB of L2 traffic for 33.7 MB of experts). Now lane l loads word l of each tile once
(one 128-byte warp load a 4-bit tile) and takes its windows' words from their owners by __shfl_sync; the next tile's
words and its A fragment are issued a tile ahead (warp_tiles_shfl). At 4 bits the windows sit at fixed nibble offsets
(lane_states8: funnel shifts and one byte_perm), and the mcg mask is kept in a register (ptxas rebuilt it with a MOV for
every LOP3: 26 of the k step's 252 instructions; now 216). Same words, same A values, same decoded values, same MMA
chain over the same k tiles, same warp-order sum: the same bits.

- exl3_grouped.cuh: Load SHFL (+ planted faults SHFL_SRC, SHFL_A), lane_states8, decode2_mcg, warp_tiles_shfl;
  grouped_body_v2 takes it at one trellis width.
- exl3_experts.cu: tf_exl3_grouped_1_k8r8s (<= 8 rows) and _k8r16s (9-32 rows), SHFL on sm_120 up, main's loop below.
- exl3_experts.zig: tilesFor gives every loader-verified 4-bit mcg projection the read-once kernels for windows up to
  32 rows (before: k8r8 to 8 rows, nt4 to 32); TF_EXL3_SHFL=0 restores the old choice (same bits either way).

Measured [M, exl3r bench, RTX PRO 6000, 400 W, cold 4-bit experts, trains of 8 back-to-back calls, medians, GPU1]:
gate/up -1.1/-5.0/-3.0/-10.5/-12.4/-14.0% and down -1.7/-1.2/-7.1/-6.0/-13.7/-14.0% at 1/2/4/8/16/32 rows (gate/up plus
down -1.3/-3.6/-4.5/-9.0/-12.8/-14.0%). Exactness: 0 of 288 cells differ from the old kernels (rows 1-32,
random/NaN/inf/large inputs, every row on the same experts); both planted faults caught in 72 of 72 cells.

